        {
          "id": "scm_call120_cirrus_ice_only_layers_20_59",
          "description": "Reference: WRF 4.8 em_scm_xy single-column run (GNU real32 build, dt = 60 s, 59 layers, mp = 6), call 120 (20:00 UTC) dumped by the instrumented ctessum-claude/WRF fork (module_esm_dump with esm_dump_inner hooks inside mp_wsm6_run of the ctessum-claude/MMM-physics fork, commit 52cfbd7) and replayed through the real64 (kind_phys = real64) standalone kernels/wsm6_driver. INPUTS are the kernel's input state (t, qi, qr, qs, qg, den, delz of tile column 1), i.e. the state the fallout block sees at the start of the sub-step. REFERENCE FLUXES are Fortran-derived: the kernel's fall arrays (fall(:,k,:) = post-fallout density x fall speed / delz for k >= 2, and the semi-Lagrangian surface precipitation / delz / dtcld at k = 1), multiplied by delz, from three real64 replays at ESM_DT = 0.04, 0.02, 0.01 s and Richardson-extrapolated to dt -> 0 (second order; the kernel's fluxes converge linearly in dt to the donor-cell fluxes rho v_t q, so the extrapolation removes the residual to ~1e-12 relative). REFERENCE TENDENCIES are the FORMULA, not the Fortran: (F[k+1] - F[k])/(rho[k] dz[k]) with F[NLEV+1] = 0, evaluated by the filler on the extrapolated fluxes; WSM6's own fallout increment is a forward semi-Lagrangian PLM step (nislfv_rain_plm/plm6) that is not rate x dt: at the WRF step (dt = 60 s) the PLM increment/dt differs from this donor-cell divergence layer by layer by factors nan-nan for rain (Linf relative difference nan% over the layers carrying more than 0.1 % of the peak divergence), and the PLM surface precipitation rate is 0 vs the donor-cell 0 kg m^-2 s^-1; as dt -> 0 both converge to the values asserted here. Cloud-ice fluxes have no kernel counterpart above the surface (fallc is dumped only at k = 1), so F_i and dqi_dt are checked against the same formulae evaluated by the filler on the input state (N_i = min(max(5.38e7 (rho q_i)^0.75, 1e3), 1e6), D = min(dicon sqrt(rho q_i/N_i), dimax), v_i = 1.49e4 D^1.31) -- a wiring check, not an independent reference. Real64 replay fluxes agree with the real32 in-model fall arrays to ~2e-6 relative (the dumped pvtr/pvts/pvtg are real32). Residual esm-vs-extrapolated mismatch (real32 constants and default-real literals of the kernel, FORTRAN_BUGS.md N2; measured with zero tolerances): fluxes and tendencies <= 1.1e-7 of each column's maximum (rain 8.8e-8, snow 1.1e-7, graupel 1.1e-7, ice 1.0e-7), surface rates 1.1-1.3e-7 relative -- the same floor as the rate models (the kernel's real32 pvtr/pvts/pvtg, bvtr = 0.800000011920929, den0, 1.49e4, 1.31 and 5.38e7 versus the exact esm constants); column tolerances are 1e-6 of each reference column's maximum (Linf_error), scalar tolerances rel 2e-6, i.e. 5-10x above. Tolerances are set 5-10x above. Regime: SCM cirrus column, WRF layers 20-59 (the component's 40-layer window; the window's lowest face is the top of layer 19, where the kernel's interior flux fall(:,20,:) delz applies as the donor flux): only cloud ice (<= 4.6e-5 kg/kg in layers 50-57) is present, so the rain, snow and graupel fluxes, tendencies and precipitation are exactly zero and the ice tendency is checked by the formula.",
